  "benchmark": "A frozen learned policy plays at least 100,000 fresh 200bb HUNL Slumbot hands, scores above 0 bb/100, and has a 95% confidence-interval lower bound above 0.",
  "hypothesis": "The fixed outcome-blind multiplier 1 - posterior_entropy/log(6) will preserve nonnegative training-domain and both-seat performance while repairing unseen breadth: both frozen seeds and both seats remain nonnegative versus Standard10, holdout shrunk-minus-base is nonnegative, and shrinkage improves holdout reward versus the unshrunk checkpoint on fresh common decks.",
  "material_change": "Add inference-only posterior reliability power=1 without changing learned tensors. Hash-load both frozen recovery checkpoints and the classifier, generate wholly fresh 64-hand contexts and 128 common-deck pairs for every nine-policy/two-seat cell, and compare Standard10, unshrunk, and reliability-shrunk arms. No reward-based multiplier search and no training updates.",
