  "notes": [
    "Power=1 is fixed from the outcome-blind feasibility result. The control will not scan powers or select checkpoints from these rewards. Paired-deck units average seats before primary CIs.",
    "Both 8,064-hand seed evidence files completed before a postprocessing-only failure. The original aggregation omitted seed_index from its pair key; recovery added seed_index and recomputed all metrics from unchanged SHA-frozen JSONL with zero regenerated hands.",
    "All preregistered pooled gates passed, but seed1 holdout was unchanged by shrinkage and remained -0.456 bb/100. Therefore the multiplier is admitted as a conservative OOD control, not as replicated holdout improvement."
  ],
  "result": {
    "summary": "Across 16,128 fresh evaluation hands, fixed entropy reliability changed the two frozen policies from pooled -3.792 bb/100 unshrunk to +3.472 ±4.920 shrunk. Holdouts improved from -13.125 to +0.879 ±5.226 and training domains remained +4.769; both seeds and seats had nonnegative shrunk pooled point estimates.",
    "conclusion": "Outcome-blind entropy shrinkage materially reduces OOD downside while preserving the learned contextual signal. Its effect is seed-heterogeneous, so it supports a conservative geometric learning-curve expansion with multiple seeds and frozen checkpoints, not a strength claim or Slumbot gate.",
    "decision": "ADMIT_RELIABILITY_SHRUNK_CONTEXTUAL_GEOMETRIC_CURVE",
    "next_step": "Train three new posterior-centered seeds on a preregistered 4x geometric curve with frozen checkpoints at the current 128 and 512 learning-hands-per-group doses; evaluate every endpoint with reliability power=1 on new broad common decks, tracking seed slopes, holdout breadth, both seats, and Standard10 preservation."
  },
